CORE smt-backend gcc-only no-new-smt broken-cprover-smt-backend
symbolic-unequal.c
--cvc5 --external-smt2-solver ./cvc5-mbqi.sh
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a\[1\] and b\[1\] may differ: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ a and b may be equal: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The solver must be able to produce models when arrays of non-constant size are
compared using a bounded quantifier. For the second assertion, the model must
satisfy the quantified formula, which cvc5 only reports as "sat" when using
model-based quantifier instantiation (--mbqi): without it, cvc5 returns
"unknown". CBMC does not pass --mbqi to cvc5 by default as it changes cvc5's
performance considerably, hence the wrapper script. This test is marked
"gcc-only" as resolving ./ won't work with Windows.
